      "id": "info-note",
      "name": "Workflow Info",
      "parameters": {
        "color": 4,
        "content": "# 📧 Automated Email Management System\n\n## Overview\nThis workflow automatically processes incoming emails using AI to categorize and organize them efficiently.\n\n## Features\n✅ Auto-categorizes emails into 7 categories\n✅ Moves junk/spam to Junk folder\n✅ Organizes receipts separately\n✅ Marks processed emails as read\n✅ Runs every 15 minutes automatically\n\n## Categories\n• Action - Requires immediate attention\n• Junk - Spam/promotional content\n• Business - Work communications\n• SaaS - Software notifications\n• Receipt - Purchase confirmations\n• Newsletter - Periodic updates\n• Personal - Non-work emails\n\n## Setup Required\n1. Connect Microsoft Outlook account\n2. Configure AI model (Ollama/OpenAI)\n3. Set up target folders in Outlook\n4. Test with sample emails first",
        "height": 480,
        "width": 400
      },
      "position": [
        -600,
        100
      ],
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "setup-note",
      "name": "Setup Instructions",
      "parameters": {
        "color": 5,
        "content": "# ⚙️ Setup Instructions\n\n## Step 1: Microsoft Outlook Connection\n1. Click on any Outlook node\n2. Create new credentials\n3. Authorize your Outlook account\n4. Note down folder IDs for Junk and Receipts\n\n## Step 2: AI Model Configuration\n1. Set up Ollama server locally or use OpenAI\n2. Configure the AI model connection\n3. Test with a sample prompt\n\n## Step 3: Folder Setup\n1. Create \"Receipts\" folder in Outlook\n2. Get folder ID (use Outlook REST API)\n3. Update folder IDs in move nodes\n\n## Step 4: Testing\n1. Use manual trigger first\n2. Send test emails to each category\n3. Verify categorization accuracy\n4. Adjust prompts if needed\n\n## Tips\n• Start with conservative AI settings\n• Monitor first few runs closely\n• Fine-tune categories based on results\n• Consider adding more specific categories",
        "height": 520,
        "width": 400
      },
      "position": [
        -600,
        600
      ],
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1
